{
  "$comment": [
    "Researched skeleton for the Taurus (Toros) options, late October 2026.",
    "",
    "Each day is a chain of control points on real roads: towns, junctions and passes,",
    "with the elevation each of them actually sits at. `targetKm` and `targetAscentM`",
    "are the researched road distance and climbing for the day — they are NOT measured",
    "off the line below, which is a straight-segment skeleton and therefore shorter.",
    "",
    "scripts/build-taurus-gpx.mjs turns this into the committed GPX. In `sketch` mode it",
    "densifies the skeleton and calibrates it to the targets, which is what is committed",
    "today; with --brouter it re-routes every leg over OpenStreetMap instead, which is",
    "what should replace it before anyone books a flight. See docs/taurus-2026.md."
  ],
